ken the best possible  public health advice  scientific advice we have the best  advisors in the world  and and together looking at the impact  of the vaccine and the severe weakening  of that link  we of course are very comfortable with  the decisions  that were announced now i fully  understand why many people  will be anxious they'd want to be  cautious and that is why  other protections remain in place but  the the vaccines  are working and if i can just quickly  just share an example of  why i'm saying that is that you're at  the moment here in the last 24 hours  we're getting case numbers around over  25 000  a day but when you look at  hospitalizations  and deaths your deaths for example are 1  30th of what they were the last time we  saw  case numbers of that type and and also  when we're thinking about our health  challenges and health problems  one of the things i tried to set out  yesterday as well is as health secretary  i'm also  very concerned about all the non-covered  health problems which you know they  haven't gone away  and if anything they've got a lot worse  you know the waiting list  has grown dramatically it's going to  grow a lot more before it comes back  down again  sadly there are many people that have  not come forward  with cancer problems with heart disease  problems with mental health problems  and i'm very concerned about that too  minister i i completely i completely  understand that i'm not going to ask the  question again whether or not face masks  are affected because we know that they  are  in the latest meta-analysis that came  out in the last 24 hours six million  individuals involved in it  shows that it reduces transmission by  the very least 25 percent  so i'm just wondering about the the  shift that we have seen between  last thursday and yesterday evening in  which you know we're not being told what  to do anymore we've been given  personal responsibility to to make our  own decisions  on that basis in which circumstances 